%I A037652 #27 Sep 20 2026 17:41:40
%S A037652 3,30,301,3013,30130,301301,3013013,30130130,301301301,3013013013,
%T A037652 30130130130,301301301301,3013013013013,30130130130130,
%U A037652 301301301301301,3013013013013013,30130130130130130,301301301301301301,3013013013013013013,30130130130130130130
%N A037652 Decimal expansion of a(n) is given by the first n terms of the periodic sequence with initial period 3,0,1.
%H A037652 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (10,0,1,-10).
%F A037652 G.f.: x*(3+x^2) / ( (x-1)*(10*x-1)*(1+x+x^2) ). - _R. J. Mathar_, Aug 04 2013
%F A037652 From _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 20 2026: (Start)
%F A037652 a(n) = floor((301/999)*10^n).
%F A037652 a(n) = 10*a(n-1) + a(n-3) - 10*a(n-4). (End)
%F A037652 E.g.f.: exp(-x/2)*(301*exp(21*x/2) - 148*exp(3*x/2) - 153*cos(sqrt(3)*x/2) + 39*sqrt(3)*sin(sqrt(3)*x/2))/999. - _Stefano Spezia_, Sep 20 2026
%p A037652 a:= proc(n) option remember; `if`(n=0, 0,
%p A037652       a(n-1)*10+[3, 0, 1][irem(n-1, 3)+1])
%p A037652     end:
%p A037652 seq(a(n), n=1..20);  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Sep 20 2026
%o A037652 (PARI) Vec(x*(3+x^2)/((x-1)*(10*x-1)*(1+x+x^2)) + O(x^25)) \\ _Jinyuan Wang_, Apr 14 2020
%K A037652 nonn,base,easy,changed
%O A037652 1,1
%A A037652 _Clark Kimberling_
%E A037652 More terms from _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 20 2026
